SELECT 'Freshdesk Freddy', 'freshdesk.com', 'compliant_with_caveats', '"By using the AI Services, unless Customer opts-out as further set forth below and in the Documentation Customer grants Freshworks a royalty-free license to use its Customer Data and AI Output for AI Training and expressly consents to such AI Training." "Freshworks will not use or permit Customer Data to train third party hosted generative AI models, including Microsoft Azure Open AI." Training is on by default once a business uses Freshworks'' AI Services (Freddy AI in Freshdesk). Section 4(d) of the Supplemental Terms gives two opt-out levels, both by emailing support@freshworks.com: “Opt Out of Training Collaborative Models”, which keeps the AI Services working, or “Opt Out of All AI Training”, which covers both Collaborative and Custom Models. Freshworks says training stops within seven business days of the opt-out notice, and its training licence expires 180 days after the business terminates the AI Services or opts out. Only the business that holds the Freshworks account can opt out; end users and people who contact a company''s Freshdesk helpdesk can''t opt out themselves. Customer data isn''t used to train third-party hosted generative models. Where Freshworks'' Freddy AI FAQ describes the opt-out differently, the Supplemental Terms take precedence. Source: Freshworks Supplemental Terms (Effective Date March 6, 2026), checked 17 November 2026; Freshworks'' legal pages cover Freshdesk.', NULL, 1, NULL, '["https://www.freshworks.com/terms/supplemental-terms/"]', 1, 0, 0, '2026-11-17T09:42:00.000Z', 1, 1, 0
